        System.out.println(imageElement.getDocument().getDocumentElement());
    }
}
```

In this example, we create an `Attributes` class that holds a list of `Attribute` objects. The `createImageElement` method creates a new HTML `img` element and sets its `src` attribute to the provided value. It also adds any attributes from the provided `Attributes` object.

Please note that you will need to implement the `addProtocols` method in the `Attribute` class as it's not implemented in this example.

Also, please note that this is a very basic implementation and doesn't cover all edge cases. For production use, consider using an existing library or framework for creating HTML elements.
